# Local setup: uv sync --dev; copy this file to .env and fill the secrets.
# Export with: set -a; . ./.env; set +a
# Collect: uv run autodom sync --pages 3
# Start: uv run autodom run
# Docker/Coolify: docker compose up -d --build (one replica only).
# Status: uv run autodom status
# Backup/restore commands and safe-new-directory usage: uv run autodom --help
# This file is not loaded automatically by the Python process.
# Leave token unset to read it from: pass show autodom/telegram/bot-token
AUTODOM_BOT_TOKEN=
AUTODOM_DATA_DIR=.local
AUTODOM_REFRESH_SECONDS=300
AUTODOM_REFRESH_PAGES=3
AUTODOM_CRAWL_DELAY=2
AUTODOM_FULL_REFRESH_SECONDS=86400
AUTODOM_MONITOR_SECONDS=30
AUTODOM_BACKUP_DIR=.local/backups

# Prepared foreign adapters remain OFF until source permission is obtained.
# This allowlist gates collection, search, and notification delivery, including
# foreign records that were previously imported into a database.
AUTODOM_APPROVED_SOURCES=mashina.kg
# After permission, explicitly add encar.com and/or truecar.com to the allowlist.
# Encar scope: Korean domestic brands, not an export-ready inventory.
# TrueCar's verified sample: Toyota Camry, site-default ZIP 10017 / 75 miles.
# This is NOT a nationwide feed. Validate any changed URL/scope after permission.
AUTODOM_TRUECAR_SEARCH_URL=https://www.truecar.com/used-cars-for-sale/listings/toyota/camry/
# Terms: https://fem.encar.com/policy/terms and https://www.truecar.com/terms/
# Do not enable a crawler merely because an anonymous HTTP request succeeds.
#
# /edit collects market (when multiple are approved), currency, budget, and models,
# then requires explicit Save on a review screen. Optional filters can be skipped.
# Original KRW uses whole won; USD/KGS use cents/tyiyn. NBKR daily/weekly XML
# supplies dated conversions. Missing/expired FX does not imply a usable price.
# No delivery, duty, paperwork, repair, or guaranteed export costs are invented.
# Status now reports each source's own last update, error, and observed scope.
# Review fields: source city (not delivery city), body, earliest listed year,
# maximum km, transmission, import willingness, purpose, and planned purchase date.
# Unknown source characteristics fail a selected hard filter; miles are converted
# exactly before applying whole-kilometer caps. Cities compare normalized words.
# Purpose/date are advisory, not suitability scores or monitoring stop deadlines.
# Changing currency in review requires a new amount; Back retains the old budget.
# "Total" budget excludes foreign offers until landed costs can be calculated;
# local asking-price matches are also preliminary, not a full-cost guarantee.
# Existing databases upgrade to schema 4 and backfill search columns once.
# Old profiles keep their behavior; preferences, quiet hours, and cursors persist.
# Offline regression suite (no inventory requests): uv run pytest -q

# Copy Domcom's existing secrets into local/Coolify environment, never into Git.
# Primary: datacenter. Fallback: active residential ISP pool used by Domcom.
# Both routes are required; there is no direct-network fallback.
SMARTPROXY_USERNAME=
SMARTPROXY_PASSWORD=
SMARTPROXY_DATACENTER_ENDPOINT=dc.decodo.com:10001
SMARTPROXY_DATACENTER_PORT_START=10001
SMARTPROXY_DATACENTER_PORT_COUNT=1000
SMARTPROXY_RESIDENTIAL_USERNAME=
SMARTPROXY_RESIDENTIAL_PASSWORD=
SMARTPROXY_RESIDENTIAL_ENDPOINT=isp.decodo.com:10001
SMARTPROXY_RESIDENTIAL_PORT_START=10001
SMARTPROXY_RESIDENTIAL_PORT_COUNT=10

# /delete removes active user state immediately. Private local snapshots expire
# within seven days; local snapshots are not protection against losing the server.
